{"study_accession":"PRJNA1073495","secondary_study_accession":"SRP488177","title":"Transcriptomic analysis of plasma extracellular vesicles from patients with ischemic stroke of different etiologies undergoing mechanical thrombectomy","description":"INTRODUCTION: Accurate ischemic stroke (IS) etiologic diagnosis provides an appropriate secondary prevention strategy and better outcome. Currently, 45% of IS are cryptogenic urging to find novel approaches to enhance diagnostic precision and secondary stroke prevention. OBJETIVE: To study the transcriptomic content of circulating extracellular vesicles (EVs) to delineate the molecular profile and potential biomarkers of IS etiologies. RESULTS:21 consecutive patients with moderate or severe ischemic stroke (IS) and different IS etiologies were included to perform the transcriptomic analysis of plasma EVs comprising: atherothrombotic (AT, n=6), Cardioembolic (CE, n=10), and embolic stroke of undetermined source (ESUS, n=5). The RNASeq analysis of EVs detected clusters of differentially expressed genes (DEGs) related to IS etiologies. Overall design: Transcriptome of patients with ischemic stroke of atherothrombotic (AT, n=6), cardioembolic (CE, n=10) or undetermined etiology (ESUS, n=5) were compared in circulating extracellular vesicles .","pubmed":"38673963","geo_series":"","n_samples":21,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN39831657","study_accession":"PRJNA1073495","blood_class":"plasma_serum_cfrna","class_from":"sample","title":"Cardio_10","description":"Cardio_10","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM8063828","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2024-05-26","attributes":[["source_name","Plasma circulating extracellular vesicles"],["tissue","Plasma circulating extracellular vesicles"],["is etiology","cardioembolic"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR27873208","experiment_accession":"SRX23535141","library_layout":"SINGLE","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_